[Audio:start-up-tune:Start-up Tune]
Played by #R$BDFE each time a new game is started.
The music data is at #R$C7F8.

#AUDIO0(start-up-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(StartUpTune))

[Audio:main-tune:Main Tune]
Played by #R$C8CA while the game selection menu is shown, until a key is
pressed.
The music data is at #R$C770.

#AUDIO0(main-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(MainTune))

[Audio:menu-selection-tune:Menu Selection Tune]
Played by #R$C8CA each time an option on the game selection menu is changed.
The music data is at #R$C7F4.

#AUDIO0(menu-selection-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(MenuSelectionTune))

[Audio:life-lost-tune:Life Lost Tune]
Played by #R$CBAC when the player has died and has a life left.
The music data is at #R$C839.

#AUDIO0(life-lost-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(LifeLostTune))

[Audio:game-over-tune:Game Over Tune]
Played by #R$CC56 when the game is over.
The music data is at #R$C803.

#AUDIO0(game-over-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(GameOverTune))

[Audio:game-complete-tune:Game Complete Tune]
Played by #R$CD10 when all four monsters have been killed and the ending is
over.
The music data is at #R$C81A.

#AUDIO0(game-complete-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(GameCompleteTune))

[Audio:ghost-sound:Ghost Sound]
Played by #R$BFF1 each frame that a ghost is in view.
The pitch comes from the frame counter, so here the sixteen pitches of #R$C34D
are used one after the other.

#AUDIO0(ghost-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(GhostSound))

[Audio:monster-sound:Monster Sound]
Played by #R$D94F each frame that a monster is in view.
The pitch comes from the frame counter and the kind of monster. The game
reads the pitches from the ROM (see #R$C34D), so here the four kinds of
monster are used one after the other.

#AUDIO0(monster-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(MonsterSound))

[Audio:ending-ghost-sound:Ending Ghost Sound]
Played by #R$CD58 for each frame that a ghost moves on the ending screen.
The tone gets lower each time it is played, so here it is played thirty-two
times.

#AUDIO0(ending-ghost-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(EndingGhostSound))

[Audio:bump-sound:Bump Sound]
Played by #R$C083 when a creature bumps into something and by #R$DA00 when the
legs of the player bump into something.
Sixteen short tones.

#AUDIO0(bump-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(BumpSound))

[Audio:new-cell-sound:New Cell Sound]
Played by #R$BDFE, one note for each pass of the main loop, after #R$BF48 has
started it when the player enters a cell that holds something other than open
ground for the first time.
Four notes, with a pause between each of them.

#AUDIO0(new-cell-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(NewCellSound))

[Audio:speed-bonus-sound:Speed Bonus Sound]
Played by #R$BDFE, one note for each pass of the main loop, after #R$D727 has
started it when the player touches a speed bonus.
Five notes, with a pause between each of them.

#AUDIO0(speed-bonus-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(SpeedBonusSound))

[Audio:health-bonus-sound:Health Bonus Sound]
Played by #R$BDFE, one note for each pass of the main loop, after #R$D74C has
started it when the player touches a health bonus.
Seven notes, with a pause between each of them.

#AUDIO0(health-bonus-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(HealthBonusSound))

[Audio:item-sound:Item Sound]
Played by #R$BDFE, one note for each pass of the main loop, after #R$D942 has
started it when the player picks up an item that a monster needs.
Four notes, with a pause between each of them.

#AUDIO0(item-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(ItemSound))

[Audio:throw-sound:Throw Sound]
Played by #R$DAB7 when the player throws an item.
A sweep of thirty-two single cycles. The pitch comes from the place in the
inventory that the item was thrown from, so here the eleven places are used
one after the other.

#AUDIO0(throw-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(ThrowSound))

[Audio:footstep-sound:Footstep Sound]
Played by #R$DCA8 as the player walks.
A tick, alternately high and low, every four frames (every two frames when
the player is moving quickly). Here the player takes sixteen steps.

#AUDIO0(footstep-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(FootstepSound))

[Audio:explosion:Explosion]
Played by #R$D7D8 when a burst has finished.
Sixteen short bursts of a tone, with pitches from a random place in the ROM.
The game picks the place at random, so here it is fixed.

#AUDIO0(explosion.wav)(#INCLUDE(Explosion))

[Audio:ball-sound:Ball Sound]
Played by #R$C164 for each frame that a ball is in view.
The pitch comes from the type of the ball, so here the four frames are used
one after the other.

#AUDIO0(ball-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(BallSound))

[Audio:appearing-sound:Appearing Sound]
Played by #R$DA7A for each frame while the player is materialising.
The pitch comes from the materialise timer, so here the timer runs from
#N$28 to #N$6E.

#AUDIO0(appearing-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(AppearingSound))
